1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:04,100
Um, so your morning routine keeps falling apart?

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,900
It's probably not because you're lazy.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,600
Here are three reasons it keeps failing.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,500
Reason one is, uh, you copied

5
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:18,800
Reason one is you copied someone else's routine. A 5 a.m. wake-up, cold plunge, journaling, the whole thing.

6
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:22,400
But you're not them. Your mornings, like, look completely different.

7
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:27,600
So start with one thing that already fits your actual morning.

8
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:31,200
Reason two: you made it way too long.

9
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:35,900
If your routine needs ninety minutes, it will die the first time you oversleep.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,800
Basically, keep a ten-minute version for bad days. Um, the non-negotiable version.

11
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:44,800
And reason three, which nobody talks about:

12
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:49,200
your routine starts the night before. Not when your alarm goes off.

13
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,600
If you scroll until one a.m., no routine in the world is going to save you.

14
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:57,400
So you know, pick a phone-down time and protect it like a meeting.

15
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:02,800
Quick recap: make it yours, make it short, and start the night before.

16
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:06,400
Save this for tomorrow morning, and follow for more calm habits.
